3.how many releases happens-in a week/month?
“In our team, we follow a continuous delivery model, so releases are quite frequent.”

On average, we do around 5 to 15 releases per week.
Small bug fixes and configuration changes are released daily through our automated CI/CD pipelines.

For major features, we usually plan 1 or 2 structured releases per week.
Before production, we deploy to staging, run validations, and then push using canary or blue-green deployments.

If there is any production issue, we also do hotfix releases immediately to minimize business impact.

Because we follow small, incremental releases,

risk is low

rollback is easy

and recovery is faster.
